The person who is "responsible" for maintaining and distributing the hack
sources, namely Andries Brouwer, is in Denmark temporarily and has been for
quite a while now.  I sent mail to him about a couple of bugs I found and was
extremely surprised to learn that I was the first to successfully do so since
he released version 1.0.3.

He informed me that he doesn't have regular access to USENET and that mail was
being lost during the past three or four months and he asked me to bring this
to your attention.  So, if you mailed him during that time, you may want to try
again.  Mail to his "official" address, namely "mcvax!aeb", still works and is
temporarily forwarded to the machine he actually uses.

If you report bugs just by posting an article, therefore, it is possible that
he will never see it.

By the way, I was wielding 9 rocks against an acid blob and got the message
"the 9 rocks corrode"?!
